{"id": "EUVD-2026-104400", "enisaUuid": "cf06ded0-e84e-3785-953b-623afaef33a7", "description": "crewai-tools through 1.15.28 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability in SeleniumScrapingTool that allows attackers to fetch internal resources because it never applies the validate_url private-address check. Attackers influencing agent tool input through prompt injection can direct headless Chrome to loopback, RFC1918, or cloud metadata addresses to disclose internal data and cloud credentials.", "datePublished": "2026-10-19T15:28:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T18:23:27", "baseScore": 8.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:P/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:H/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/pull/6870", "https://github.com/crewAIInc/crewAI/blob/1.15.28/lib/crewai-tools/src/crewai_tools/tools/selenium_scraping_tool/selenium_scraping_tool.py", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/crewai-tools-through-1.15.28-ssrf-via-seleniumscrapingtool"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5595-9g9c-5cc4", "CVE-2026-112308"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.24, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "2709b0f4-c0af-3373-bdf8-2d766ec4c6a4", "product": {"name": "crewai-tools", "vendor": {"name": "crewAIInc"}}, "product_version": "0 \u22641.15.28"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "8def4326-9d91-3a75-8d92-a6749835cc6a", "vendor": {"name": "crewAIInc"}}], "isExploited": false}